Findings
--------
F1r3 [Blocker]: forms 12 and 13. oxlint honors both CRLF // forms, the pin
counts both, but TRAILING_DISABLE_RE (:905) has no multiline flag and its
.* cannot cross a carriage return, so stripDisableComments (:913-915)
keeps the directive verbatim and the sweep copy stays clean. A listed CRLF
carrier whose entry records no hidden rules (6 of the 49 entries do) can
hide a live finding behind either form and pass every clause of adv 7
silently. No real carrier uses CRLF today (byte scan of all 49 entries),
so the hole is latent, the state F1r2 held when it was ruled a Blocker.
Committed failing guard: adv 10 (:1672).

F2r3 [Major]: form 14. BLOCK_COMMENT_RE spans from the in-string /* to
the real disable's */, so the strip deletes the code between them and
breaks the string. The copy reports only 'error: Unterminated string';
the hidden finding never surfaces, and the decode (:1397) reads the parse
error as a rule named Unterminated. The guard fails loudly with a
misleading diagnostic today, but the natural fixture response (recording
Unterminated in hiddenRules) would pass the guard while the true hidden
rule stays unverified, which widens the fixture through the path F2r2
left unanchored. Committed failing guard: adv 11 (:1738).

F3r3 [Nit]: forms 8 to 11. The pin counts disable text that oxlint
ignores (a // line inside a block comment counts twice). Conservative
direction: such a file is flagged as a carrier and nothing hides behind
the text. Default disposition: accept.

F4r3 [Nit]: forms 15 and 16. The strip removes every disable globally, so
the copy also surfaces live faults that sit above the first disable or
after an eslint-enable, and the decode marks them as hidden. Both classes
stay visible to the workspace lint gate itself, so no silent hole exists.
Default disposition: accept and document.

Verified-good forms 1 to 7 are pinned as the passing adv 12, so a
regression on any spelling reopens the F1r2 hole visibly.

